---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Article from '../components/Article.astro';

const pageTitle = "Editorial Policy - GST Calculator Online";
const pageDesc = "Our editorial policy explains how gstcalculatoronline.in creates, reviews, and updates GST calculators, articles, and guides. Learn about our standards.";
---
<Layout seo={{ title: pageTitle, description: pageDesc }}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <Breadcrumbs />

    <Article title="Editorial Policy" date="Last Updated: July 18, 2026">

      <p><strong>GST Calculator Online</strong> (gstcalculatoronline.in) is committed to providing accurate, current, and trustworthy information about India's Goods and Services Tax (GST) system. This Editorial Policy explains how we create, review, update, and maintain our calculators, articles, and guides.</p>

      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>Our mission is to make GST compliance simpler for Indian businesses, freelancers, traders, and Chartered Accountants. Every piece of content published on this site is created with a focus on accuracy, clarity, and practical utility.</p>

      <h2>Author Qualifications</h2>
      <p>All articles, guides, and tool explanations on gstcalculatoronline.in are authored or reviewed by qualified tax professionals:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hashmi Akbar</strong> — Senior GST &amp; Indirect Tax Specialist with extensive experience in GST advisory, corporate audits, and Input Tax Credit optimizations.</li>
        <li><strong>Anjum Mina</strong> — GST Compliance &amp; Financial Advisor who has guided 500+ businesses through GST registration, GSTR-1 &amp; 3B filings, and composition scheme conversions.</li>
        <li><strong>Mehakma</strong> — GST Legal &amp; Policy Analyst specializing in regulatory compliance, tax litigation frameworks, and complex tax dispute resolution.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Content Creation Process</h2>
      <p>Every piece of content goes through the following process before publication:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Research</strong> — Authors consult the CGST Act, SGST Acts, official CBIC circulars, GST Council press releases, and the official GST Portal (gst.gov.in).</li>
        <li><strong>Drafting</strong> — Content is written in plain, accessible English without excessive jargon. Mathematical formulas are verified with working examples.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical Review</strong> — Calculator logic is cross-verified against the relevant sections of the CGST Act (e.g., Section 47 for late fees, Section 50 for interest).</li>
        <li><strong>Editorial Review</strong> — A senior team member reviews content for accuracy, clarity, and compliance with our style guidelines.</li>
        <li><strong>Publication</strong> — Content is published with the author's name, publication date, and last updated date clearly visible.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Fact-Checking Standards</h2>
      <p>All factual claims in our articles and calculators must be supported by at least one of the following primary sources:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Official CGST Act, 2017 and state-level SGST Acts</li>
        <li>Notifications and circulars published by CBIC (cbic.gov.in)</li>
        <li>GST Council press releases and communiqués</li>
        <li>Official GST Portal (gst.gov.in) FAQs and user manuals</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Calculator Accuracy Policy</h2>
      <p>Our calculator algorithms are implemented based on the mathematical formulas prescribed in the CGST Act and verified CBIC notifications. Key policies:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Late fee calculations follow Section 47 of the CGST Act, including the rationalized turnover-based caps introduced in 2023.</li>
        <li>Interest calculations follow Section 50 of the CGST Act (18% p.a. for delayed payment, 24% p.a. for wrongly utilized ITC).</li>
        <li>GST refund estimations are based on Rule 89 of the CGST Rules, 2017.</li>
        <li>All calculator results are estimates. We strongly recommend verifying critical tax figures with a qualified CA before filing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Update Policy</h2>
      <p>The GST framework is dynamic, with the GST Council regularly amending tax slabs, caps, and procedures. Our update policy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Calculator algorithms are reviewed and updated within 15 business days of any official GST Council notification that affects our tools.</li>
        <li>Articles are reviewed on a quarterly basis or when significant policy changes occur.</li>
        <li>Every updated article or calculator page displays a "Last Updated" date to show readers the freshness of the information.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Corrections Policy</h2>
      <p>We take accuracy seriously. If you discover an error in our content or calculators, please <a href="/contact" class="text-link hover:underline">contact us</a>. We will:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Review the reported issue within 3 business days.</li>
        <li>If the error is confirmed, correct it promptly and update the "Last Updated" date on the affected page.</li>
        <li>For significant corrections that affect tax figures, add an editorial note explaining what was corrected and why.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Independence &amp; Non-Affiliation</h2>
      <p>gstcalculatoronline.in is an independent educational platform. We are <strong>not affiliated with, endorsed by, or officially connected to</strong> the GSTN, CBIC, the Ministry of Finance, or the Government of India. Our content is produced independently, and we do not receive any compensation from government bodies for our coverage.</p>

      <h2>Advertising Disclosure</h2>
      <p>This website uses Google AdSense to display relevant advertisements. Advertisements do not influence our editorial content, tool algorithms, or the information we present. Our calculators and articles are created solely on the basis of accuracy and user value — not advertiser interests.</p>

      <h2>Contact the Editorial Team</h2>
      <p>Have a question about our editorial standards or wish to report inaccurate content? Please reach out through our <a href="/contact" class="text-link hover:underline">Contact page</a>. We welcome feedback from tax professionals, students, and businesses.</p>

    </Article>
  </div>
</Layout>
